{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The wicked flee though none pursues</b> — the wicked flee, or: they flee though no wicked one pursues them, but a rustling leaf pursues them; like a young lion that dwells secure, so do the righteous trust and do not flee."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:05.504941986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}